## The reduced form: only Laurent data {#sec:redform}

Using Section~\ref{sec:nu} the leading identity can be written without any Q-function or normalisation:
$$
\sum_{ij}G^s_{ij}(\epsilon\hat\omega_1,\epsilon\hat\omega_1')\,\nu_i(\theta_1)\nu_j(\theta_2)=\epsilon^{6-k_B}\,\hat c\,\frac{\langle\varphi_u\otimes e_1|\Psi_0\rangle}{X_B}+O(\epsilon^{7-k_B}),\label{eq:limitnu}
$$
verified coefficientwise to $10^{-55}\ldots10^{-157}$ with lower orders vanishing to $10^{-62}\ldots10^{-165}$; no $M$, no $\kappa_B$ and no Q-normalisation enters. The $\nu$-series are needed only to order $3$ (top), $5$ ($(4,1,1)$, $(3,3,0)$), $4$ (octets) and $2$ (singlet), i.e. the Laurent data to order $\epsilon^3,\epsilon^5,\epsilon^4,\epsilon^2$. Table~\ref{tab:nudepth} lists the $(i,n)$ pairs that enter.

